from write_dossiers import add
def b(d,e,f=(),s='Partially addressed',k='methodological',c='high'):return dict(description=d,evidence=e,followups=list(f),status=s,kind=k,confidence=c)

add('crossmodalmap',year=2022,venue='CVPR 2022',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='CM² addresses VLN-CE with a90-degree RGB-D view, ground-truth pose, noiseless0.25m forward/15-degree turns and STOP. It predicts a language-conditioned local semantic map and a complete waypoint sequence, then delegates physical control to DD-PPO. Ground-truth pose and pretrained controller experience are material resource assumptions.',
method='§3 pp3–5: project depth into a192×192 occupancy grid with5cm cells; separately segment RGB. BERT produces M×128 text features, while a truncated ResNet18 encodes the map into N×128 tokens. Cross-attention H=softmax((YWq)(XWk)ᵀ/√128)XWv uses map queries and text keys/values. Two stacked U-Nets predict occupancy then27-category semantics, including unseen regions, trained with pixel CE against simulator semantic maps. A second cross-modal network predicts k waypoint heatmaps P̂∈R^(k×u×v) and traversed-waypoint labels, conditioned on the start heatmap. Lwp=Σi bi||P̂i−Pi||² plus waypoint-coverage CE, where bi masks waypoints outside the local map. Total loss combines map and waypoint losses in one backward pass. At inference choose the waypoint after the one closest to current pose; DD-PPO reaches it. Stop when close to the final predicted waypoint and heatmap confidence exceeds a threshold. This is language-conditioned map hallucination plus replanning, not an action-conditioned recurrent future-state simulator.',
novelty='Language informs both unobserved map completion and path prediction. Table3 isolates map attention, supporting better map/waypoint accuracy. Unlike pre-exploration topological planners, CM² builds predictions online, but it assumes true pose and privileged map-label supervision during training.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: Table1 p6 val-unseen SR34.3/SPL27.6, versus LAW35/31; ground-truth local maps give37/30.6. Table3 p7 map attention improves IoU21.2→28.3 and correct-waypoint71.1→76.5. Table4 changes stop threshold1.5→0.5m: val-seen SR49.5→52.8 while SPL45.1→41.8, demonstrating an explicit stopping/efficiency tradeoff. VERDICT: credible representation evidence, but stronger sample-efficiency claims should count pretrained DD-PPO and segmentation training; oracle-map results are not deployable performance.',
implementation='Inspected map/path model losses, map projection utilities, trainer, evaluator/controller interface, dataset labels and options. The released coverage head uses two-class cross entropy, clarifying the compact paper notation.',
code=[dict(path='models/vln_goal_predictor.py',locator='coverage_loss89–102; position_loss106–126',finding='Two-class coverage CE and visibility-masked heatmap MSE.'),dict(path='models/semantic_grid.py',locator='spatial-transform and map update methods',finding='Map construction uses pose-aligned spatial transformations.'),dict(path='datasets/util/map_utils.py',locator='projection and heatmap helpers',finding='Training labels and observations use explicit metric coordinates.'),dict(path='trainer_vln.py',locator='training loss aggregation',finding='Waypoint and map objectives are optimized together.')],
bottlenecks=[b('Language-conditioned hallucination may invent unseen semantics and local9.6m coverage excludes distant goals.','§3.4 and local map dimensions',('WS-MGMap','BEVBert','HSGM')),b('True-pose projection and fixed pretrained controller hide localization/control robustness costs.','§3.2 ground-truth pose assumption',(),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='operating assumption')],followups=['https://github.com/PeihaoChen/WS-MGMap','https://github.com/Teacher-Tom/HSGM_public'])

add('weakmap',year=2022,venue='NeurIPS 2022',pages=[1,4,5,6,7,8,9,17],
problem='WS-MGMap addresses loss of object attributes in category-only maps and weak correspondence between map regions and instruction objects in continuous navigation. It assumes RGB-D, metric projection and simulator-provided training geometry/semantics.',
method='§3 pp4–6: project64-channel latent U-Net segmentation features into a100×100 grid with12cm cells. A hallucination module predicts27-category semantic occupancy; fuse fine-grained and semantic features by convolutions. A GRU encodes RGB/depth/map history, attends to BiLSTM instruction features, then computes a spatial distribution P̂ over map cells. Weak target P=softmax(P′), P′k=(dmax−dk)/(dmax−dmin), is based on distance dk to the demonstration path, not annotated object locations. Optimize KL(P||P̂). The attended map, text and first GRU state feed a second GRU; linear heads regress a2D waypoint and scalar progress. A LAW-style expert chooses a point3m along the shortest route to the nearest reference waypoint; DD-PPO executes low-level actions and STOP fires when progress>.8. L=Lsemantic+10Llocalization+10Lprogress+10Lwaypoint, with squared regression errors; teacher-forcing on150k augmented examples is followed by DAgger. Frozen segmentation/controller and2V100/3days are reported. Waypoints refresh every3steps.',
novelty='Fuses latent attribute features with hallucinated category maps and path-derived weak localization. The weak target encourages path proximity; calling it verified object grounding would exceed its supervision. Eq3 describes cosine similarity but prints an unnormalized projected dot product; the inspected attention implementation uses dot-product-style attention, so normalization assumptions should be checked before reusing the equation.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: Table3 p8 no map SR26.5/SPL21.4; fine-grained31.6/28.2; semantic33.3/28.2; fused38.9/34.3. Appendix Table7 p17 no DAgger24.6SR versus38.9 with DAgger: training distribution correction is a major contributor. VERDICT: strong complementary-feature evidence, but weak localization success does not prove correct object identity; comparison must retain data/DAgger/sensor controls.',
implementation='Inspected projected RGB-feature mapping, semantic/fine-grained fusion, dual recurrent policy, DAgger training and configuration. The source shows map attention and classifier output, supporting the stated implementation mapping.',
code=[dict(path='vlnce_baselines/models/mg_map_policy.py',locator='forward180–251',finding='Projects RGB features, predicts semantic map, concatenates map features, computes text-conditioned map attention, and updates the second recurrent state.'),dict(path='vlnce_baselines/common/rgb_mapping.py',locator='mapping update methods',finding='Builds pose-aligned projected latent-feature memory.'),dict(path='vlnce_baselines/dagger_trainer.py',locator='collection/training paths',finding='DAgger is a substantive training stage rather than an inference-only map addition.'),dict(path='vlnce_baselines/config/CMA_AUG_DA_TUNE.yaml',locator='training configuration',finding='Defines the augmented/DAgger setup needed for matched reproduction.')],
bottlenecks=[b('Path proximity is an imperfect proxy for the exact object referred to; salient objects can be off the path.','KL target §3.3',('OVER-NAV open-vocabulary detections','REVERIE explicit grounding'),k='supervision'),b('Height-collapsed fixed-resolution maps and exact-pose projection lose3D distinctions and inherit localization noise sensitivity.','§3.2 map construction',('VER','GaussianMap','GA-VLN'))],followups=['https://github.com/DefaultRui/VLN-VER','https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.17334'])

add('goat',year=2024,venue='CVPR 2024',pages=[1,3,4,5,6],
problem='GOAT targets dataset-dependent visual/language/history shortcuts in DUET-family navigation. It assumes room/keyword confounders and latent style/trajectory confounders in a structural causal model; these are modeling assumptions, not variables randomized by its benchmark.',
method='§4 pp3–6: extract RoBERTa direction/landmark dictionaries and CLIP room dictionaries labeled by BLIP VQA. Back-door-inspired features add fx(x)+Σz wzfz(z), using empirical frequencies or query-dependent attention weights. Front-door-inspired modules attend both current-input features and K-means-selected global training features, then sum the resulting expectations. A sigmoid gate mixes adjusted and original features. Language, local panorama and global/history features enter DUET-style dual-scale fusion and action CE. Contrastive cross-modal feature pooling uses normalized bidirectional batch InfoNCE between pooled language and local/global/fused embeddings, temperature t; it pretrains the representations used to build dictionaries. Reported6text/2panorama/3cross layers,CLIP-B/16,METER initialization,batch12 (5RxR/SOON),LR2e−5,max100k; dynamic speaker augmentation is also used. Inference reads learned dictionaries and predicts graph actions; it does not perform physical randomized interventions.',
novelty='The engineering contribution is dictionary-conditioned multimodal feature adjustment, contrastive pooling, and gated integration on a dual-scale graph backbone. The author’s claim of unbiased causal effects is stronger than evidence: front-door identification requires no unblocked X→M confounding, all causal X→Y paths mediated by M, and back-door blocking between M,Y by X. These assumptions are not established for learned attention/dictionaries; query-dependent weighting is not automatically the marginal P(z), and residual original-feature paths persist. Benchmark gains support useful regularization, not identification.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: §5 compares R2R,RxR-English,REVERIE,SOON and reports intervention/pooling ablations. The source README also warns speaker augmentation coupled with intervention is critical. VERDICT: compelling multimodal regularizer baseline for future causal claims, but one should test controlled counterfactual invariance and preserve task-relevant direction/landmark effects rather than treating all frequent keywords as removable nuisance.',
implementation='Inspected actual back/front dictionary operations, adaptive gates, confounder extraction and room-label preprocessing. The code confirms residual mixing and attention-based conditioning; the word do in function names does not establish causal identification.',
code=[dict(path='map_nav_src/models/vilmodel_GOAT.py',locator='lines94–162',finding='Frequency-weighted or attention-based dictionary features are added/gated with original text embeddings, including direct residual paths.'),dict(path='map_nav_src/do_utils/do_intervention.py',locator='dictionary construction/extraction routines',finding='Confounder representations are estimated from training samples, not externally randomized assignments.'),dict(path='map_nav_src/do_utils/extract_room_type.py',locator='BLIP room-type extraction',finding='Room labels are model predictions and can carry perception errors.')],
bottlenecks=[b('Causal effect identification is unverified; representation regularization can improve SR without removing the hypothesized confounding.','§3 SCM/§4 approximations; residual source path',(),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='causal identification'),b('Dictionary construction and multimodal attention add compute and depend on augmentation/backbone quality.','§4–5; official README dependency note',('Walk and Read Less token pruning',),k='compute/data')],followups=['https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1202/'])

add('gavln',year=2026,venue='CVPR 2026',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='GA-VLN reduces redundant history tokens and injects spatial geometry into a fine-tuned7B multimodal navigation model. Its input is front-view RGB-D plus pose; monocular here means a single viewing direction, not RGB-only sensing.',
method='§3 pp4–5: SigLIP patch features and frozen VGGT-1B multi-view features are projected to world coordinates with depth/pose, transformed to agent coordinates, and mean-pooled into occupied0.25m BEV cells within±10m. Correct dimensional backprojection is pworld=R(DK⁻¹[u,v,1]ᵀ)+t; printed Eq1’s3×4 transform times3-vector omits homogeneous augmentation. Each cell token bi,j=(Σv∈S v)/|S|+ei,j combines explicit visual and projected geometry features; only occupied cells remain. A two-layer4096-hidden MLP aligns VGGT features. LLaVA-Video-7B receives BEV,current view,instruction and predicts4actions per round; second round reuses BEV, refreshing it every8actions. Fine-tune all modules except VGGT for2epochs with action-token CE; visual LR5e−6,others2e−5. Data mix includesR2R-CE,RxR-CE,EnvDrop,ScaleVLN and319,022 converted SRDF trajectories, without DAgger or VQA data. NavRAG evaluation additionally fine-tunes one epoch on NavRAG-CE, so it is not zero-shot transfer.',
novelty='Compact BEV geometry tokens integrate a3D foundation encoder with an MLLM action policy. Table2 controls representation under the full data mix; Table3 repeats a restricted-data ablation without SRDF. This is a trained spatial-memory policy, not an online world model rollout planner.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: Table2 p7 baseline51.49SR/46.18SPL/342.9ms; BEV withoutVGGT59.21/53.87/212.9ms; full60.96/55.19/258.7ms. Geometry adds accuracy but costs latency relative to BEV-only. Table3 withoutSRDF reduces average tokens4003→514 and yields46.49→53.56SR; token statistics use121 training trajectories, not necessarily deployment distribution. VERDICT: useful evidence separating data and representation; stale8-action map updates, pose/depth errors and3D height collapse remain testable risks.',
implementation='Inspected frozen VGGT extraction, grid quantization, scatter-add/mean pooling, feature projection, dataset action setup and evaluation entrypoint.',
code=[dict(path='gavln/model/model_gavln.py',locator='encode_images127–261',finding='VGGT aggregation runs under no_grad; SigLIP/VGGT features share grid accumulators and are averaged only in occupied cells before MLLM projection.')],
bottlenecks=[b('Pose/depth errors misregister feature memory and mean pooling collapses height and potentially conflicting observations.','Eq1–5 and scatter-add implementation',(),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='representation/sensor'),b('BEV reused for8actions can become stale at decision points; more history is not monotonically beneficial.','§3.3;Table3 history-length saturation',('HSGM observation-triggered planning',),k='latency/feedback')],followups=['https://github.com/Teacher-Tom/HSGM_public'])

add('hsgm',year=2026,venue='CVPR 2026',title='Bridging the 2D-3D Gap: A Hierarchical Semantic-Geometric Map for Vision Language Navigation',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],authors=['Kailing Li','Tianwen Qian','Lijin Yang','Yuqian Fu','Jingyu Gong','Xiaoling Wang','Liang He'],
problem='Training-free task adaptation using a pretrained VLM to choose semantically meaningful, geometrically reachable waypoints. Inputs include front/left/right RGB-D and pose; GPT-5 and YOLO-E remain pretrained components, so training-free does not mean no learned perception or no API cost.',
method='§3 pp3–6: backproject RGB-D into a geometric point cloud, segment open-vocabulary instances with YOLO-E, and merge consistent3D instances. Build dense global and sparse local waypoint graphs after cylinder-occupancy, distance, obstacle-clearance and reachability checks; stairs use surface-normal/tilted-plane filtering. Rasterize geometry, object categories, path and completed-subtask locations into BEV, and annotate current image with waypoint IDs. A VLM decomposes instruction into ordered subtasks with pending/in-progress/done states. Each subtask has≤3motion directives and a stated termination condition. The VLM selects a waypoint/turn/STOP; A* over the observed graph minimizes sum of edge Euclidean lengths and converts the path into rotations/forward motions. Two consecutive STOP predictions are required for final completion. A timeout returns to the subtask start for another attempt. No VLN training objective is optimized; runtime updates maps and prompt history.',
novelty='Geometric waypoint validation, rasterized hierarchical maps, structured subtask management and decoupled A* control are integrated into a zero-shot VLM pipeline. Double-confirmed stopping, semantic progress bookkeeping, and timeout backtracking are explicit prior art for recovery proposals.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: Table1 p6 full R2R-CE val-unseen47.9SR/32.8SPL; RxR-CE41.8/25.1/54.9nDTW on500random English episodes. Ablations use a separate300-episode R2R subset: full51SR,withoutsubtasks42.1,withoutstructuredCoT34.0. Table4 reports backtracking triggered18.3%/19.0%, recovered-episode success30.8%/26.8%; this is conditional success, not causal recovery gain against a matched no-backtracking control. The A* ablation uses straight-line movement, so its gain does not isolate semantics from collision handling. VERDICT: strong practical baseline with expensive proprietary inference and privileged sensors; matched VLM/backbone/episode comparisons are essential.',
implementation='Official repository pinned and source downloaded for high-level agent, map construction, path planning, experiment runner and configuration. Detailed function evidence is recorded in the implementation appendix; no API calls or simulator episodes were executed.',
bottlenecks=[b('Self-reported subtask completion can be wrong; two consecutive STOP outputs share correlated model error and do not constitute independent verification.','§3.4 final double confirmation',(),s='Still unresolved in the reviewed literature',k='verification',c='medium'),b('Geometric safety holds only for the observed map and sensor/model assumptions; mapping misses and pose drift can invalidate reachability.','§3.3 cylinder/edge checks',(),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='sensor/control'),b('Runtime API cost and sampled RxR evaluation limit reproducibility/comparability.','§4.1 GPT-5 and500/300episode subsets',(),s='Shifted into another cost or limitation',k='compute/protocol')],followups=['https://github.com/Teacher-Tom/HSGM_public'])

add('ivln',year=2023,venue='CVPR 2023',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='Iterative VLN asks whether a robot can exploit persistent experience across sequential instructions in the same building. Episodes form tours rather than independent resets. The protocol includes an oracle correction to the true goal and transport to the next start while the agent passively observes; this is meaningful additional supervision/experience.',
method='§3 pp3–4 constructs tours by approximately solving an asymmetric traveling-salesperson ordering over existing R2R paths, using connectivity partitions and a Lin–Kernighan heuristic. t-nDTW computes exp(−DTW(Rtour,Qtour)/(|Rtour|dth)), forbids cross-episode alignment by infinite costs, excludes oracle transport, then averages tours weighted by episode count. This discourages sacrificing one episode for unlimited exploration. TourHAMT keeps up to50previous steps with boundary tokens; TourCMA retains a visual GRU state; pooling variants store max-pooled latent history. MAP-CMA projects semantics/occupancy into a persistent metric map, crops14×64×64 tensors, encodes to128×4×4, and replaces CMA RGB inputs. Training distinguishes episodic/iterative/known maps and ground-truth/RedNet semantics. Latent baselines use teacher forcing with episode-truncated gradients; map models additionally use augmented pretraining, progress loss and DAgger. Inference persists maps across episodes but resets instruction-specific state.',
novelty='Persistent multi-episode benchmark and tour-level metric, with controlled memory-reset variants. The main scientific result is that naive longer latent history can hurt while explicit map reuse helps; it is not evidence that all unstructured memories fundamentally fail.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: §5.1 extending pretrained HAMT history roughly halves t-nDTW without adequate adaptation. §5.2 iterative map evaluation improves3–4t-nDTW over episodic resets when trained for iteration. Authors explicitly acknowledge map versus CMA comparisons are confounded by DAgger training and identify ground-truth/known-map variants as invalid leaderboard submissions. VERDICT: useful persistent-memory testbed, but oracle inter-episode correction and static scenes differ from autonomous lifelong deployment.',
implementation='Official project links both discrete Bill1235813/IVLN and continuous jacobkrantz/IVLN-CE. The latter is pinned here; map policy, mapper, iterative trainer, tour dataset, measure definitions and configuration were retrieved for phase audit.',
bottlenecks=[b('Memory contents learned under short episodic training do not automatically transfer to persistent tours.','§5.1 negative TourHAMT/TourCMA results',('OVER-NAV structured open-vocabulary memory',)),b('Persistent map gains are established under oracle corrections, static scenes and accurate pose, leaving autonomous updating/forgetting under changes insufficiently tested.','§3 oracle phases and§4maps',('Context-Nav/continual-navigation frontier audit',),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='protocol')],followups=['https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.17334','https://jacobkrantz.github.io/ivln'])

add('overnav',year=2024,venue='CVPR 2024',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='Persistent tour memory should retain instruction-relevant objects beyond the13fixed categories of IVLN’s semantic map and avoid overwhelming the navigator with raw historical observations.',
method='§3 pp3–6: GPT-3.5 extracts landmark/attribute phrases; OWL-ViT-L/14 detects them in panoramas at visited viewpoints. An Omnigraph stores viewpoint connectivity, keyword labels, confidence and headings across episodes. For discrete HAMT, collect neighbors within3graph steps, keep highest-confidence box per keyword/viewpoint, select modal distance/direction for duplicates, and append keyword-text embeddings plus direction/distance embeddings to instruction tokens. For continuous MAP-CMA, register viewpoints when>1m from existing ones, redetect stored panoramas within.25m, collect neighbors within7m and attend from instruction to keyword-position features. Eq1 adds projected keyword CLS and angle embeddings plus distance embedding, all in the navigator’s text dimension. Train the underlying policies with IVLN hyperparameters; one3090 runs navigation and another detector. Inference has no additional per-scene weight training, but navigation models are trained and memories persist.',
novelty='Open-vocabulary semantic memory and structured egocentric retrieval extend IVLN. This is not a frozen VLM directly controlling navigation: the LLM preprocesses language, detector supplies memory, and trained HAMT/MAP-CMA predicts actions.',
results='AUTHOR EXPERIMENT: Table1 p6 IR2R unseen t-nDTW50→55 and SR56→60 over HAMT. Table2 continuous t-nDTW47→50 with SR35unchanged, illustrating path-fidelity improvement without endpoint gain. Table3 p7 full open vocabulary55 versus fixed-category52; TypeIII56 uses a second evaluation pass without clearing memory, explicitly privileged repeated exposure. Table4 retrieval radius3best, larger neighborhoods hurt. VERDICT: credible structured-memory gain, but duplicate-keyword modal aggregation discards instance identity and scene changes are not tested.',
implementation='Official executable implementation was not located in the bounded paper/project search. Underlying HAMT and IVLN-CE were inspected separately; their availability does not count as inspection of OVER-NAV modifications. Supplementary prompts and architecture details remain distinct available material to audit.',
bottlenecks=[b('Collapsing same-keyword detections to modal heading/distance can merge distinct instances and lose attribute-grounding distinctions.','§3.2 filtering algorithm',('GaussianMap semantic grouping','HSGM instance maps')),b('Persistent detections can become stale; static-tour gains do not validate changed-room/object scenarios.','IVLN setup and update rules',(),s='Uncertain because evidence is insufficient',k='environment shift')],followups=['https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.17334','https://github.com/Teacher-Tom/HSGM_public'])
